  "decision_date": "16/09/2011",
  "description": "Change of use of No 224 from A2 (financial and professional services) to A3/A5 (hot food takeaway/restaurant) in conjunction with the existing takeaway at no 226 and installation of two kitchen extract ducts",
  "site_name": "224-226",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "27/09/2011",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": null,
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "lapsed_date": "15/09/2014",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans 01 A received 08 September 2011 and 02 A received 08 September 2011  therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The use hereby permitted shall not be open to customers outside the following times 8.00am till 11.00pm",
    "Condition : 4 - Refuse storage for the premises shall comprise not more than one 1100L Eurobin waste storage bins together with separate facilities for the separation and storage of glass, metal, plastics, cardboard, food waste and other recyclable materials, which shall then be collected and taken to a suitable facility for recycling. The storage shall be made permanently available within three months of the date of this permission and no waste shall be stored outside the site other than in approved storage containers in the designated area. The lids of the Eurobin and other storage containers shall be kept shut at all times other than when waste is being emptied into them or being removed from site. Non-recyclable and perishable waste shall be removed from site no less frequently than once a week.",
    "Condition : 5 - The kitchen extract system shall be provided, before the use is brought into operation, and when at maximum operation shall not result in noise that is more than 10dB(A) below background noise levels for the site. The kitchen extract system shall include the following details:\r\na) A three-stage filtration system, including grease filters, pre-carbon filters and carbon filters, to be located inside the building.\r\nb) The point of discharge shall be a minimum of one metre above eaves level or one metre above openable windows of nearby properties.\r\nc) The ducting shall be circular.\r\nd) The ventilation duct shall terminate pointing directly upwards and shall not be fitted with a cowl.\r\ne) The fan shall be isolated from the inlet and discharge ducts using flexible couplings.\r\nf) The fan shall be mounted using anti-vibration mounts.\r\ng) The duct shall be isolated from the structure of the building using anti-vibration mouldings and suitable packing material where it passes through solid structures.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - The use hereby permitted for A3/A5 purpose shall not commence until full particulars and details of a scheme to insulate the premises against the transmission of airborne and impact sound has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given."
  ],
